# Repo-root .dockerignore — applies when build context is `.`. TWO images build that way: the
# frontend prod Dockerfile, whose `build` stage COPYs frontend/ sources (tsconfig.json,
# vite.config.ts, index.html, public/, src/) — context stays repo root for that, not for Caddy
# config any more (#926 moved the Caddyfile it bakes in from repo-root Caddyfile.prod to
# frontend/caddy/, which is already inside frontend/) — and sandbox-runner/agent-sandbox/
# Dockerfile (#855), which needs the repo-root `contract/` directory alongside its own directory's
# script files. compile-service used to be the second; #843 moved it and the engine it runs into
# the overlay, and its context moved with them to `tessary-paid`, which reads
# `tessary-paid/.dockerignore` instead of this file.

# The must-not-publish denylist (open-core D2/D4, epic 4). The root-context images are OPEN images
# and must carry only what the public export carries, so every `delete` row of
# scripts/lib/export-denylist.txt is excluded here too. `scripts/check-open-boundary.sh` rule 3
# asserts that every row is covered by a line in this file (the row itself, or a broader prefix such
# as `.github/` below), so this block is a gate rather than a convention. Keep it in the same order
# as the declaration. It is also what forced compile-service's context out of `.`: from here every
# one of its COPY sources is ignored.
#
# It is ONE line now because the denylist is one `delete` row. #1293 relocated every other denied
# path physically under tessary-paid/, and the nineteen lines that used to sit here went with them.
# READ THIS BEFORE ADDING A LINE BACK: the rule-3 assertion is one-directional — denylist row ->
# .dockerignore coverage, NEVER the reverse (that is why the pre-#1293 Caddyfile.prod lines could
# linger here harmlessly for two epics). So an over-broad line in this block excludes OPEN source
# from the backend and frontend build contexts and EVERY GATE STAYS GREEN. The two that were live
# traps at #1293 were `classifiers/` (the framework/tool_error/metric_drift/data_gen half stays
# public) and `.claude/` (launch.json stays public); both are gone from here for that reason.
tessary-paid/

# Build artifacts
**/node_modules/
**/target/
**/dist/
**/.vite/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Python virtualenvs and tool caches. These are NOT covered by any denylist row and never were —
# until #1293 they rode in on the blanket `classifiers/` line, which is gone because the open half
# of that tree publishes. `classifiers/.venv` is 1.3 GB on a machine that has run the tree's own
# documented `cd classifiers && uv sync`, and the frontend image builds from the repo root
# (docker-compose.yml `context: .`), so without these lines every `docker compose build frontend`
# uploads it to the daemon. `tessary-paid/.dockerignore` carries the same three globs for the same
# reason (compile-service/.venv alone is 229 MB).
**/.venv/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/

# VCS + editor
.git/
.github/
**/.idea/
**/.vscode/

# Logs
**/*.log
hs_err_pid*.log

# Local env (never bake into images)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Compose files (not needed inside images)
docker-compose*.yml

# Python bytecode, and the open classifier tree's gitignored run outputs. These were listed one
# glob at a time before epic 4, then rode in on the blanket `classifiers/` line, which #1293
# removed because the framework/tool_error/metric_drift/data_gen half publishes. The paths below
# mirror classifiers/.gitignore; `tessary-paid/.dockerignore` restates the experiments/ globs for
# the half that moved into the overlay.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
classifiers/**/data/
classifiers/**/artifacts/
classifiers/**/checkpoints/
classifiers/**/out/

# Misc
.DS_Store
caddy_data/
caddy_config/
